## Why This Is Asked

This question tests practical understanding of end-to-end streaming pipelines, data quality, and data privacy basics in a beginner-friendly AWS DVA context. It emphasizes real-world concerns like in-flight redaction, idempotent writes, and observability.

## Key Concepts

- AWS DVA: Kinesis, Lambda preprocessing, DynamoDB dedupe, S3 Parquet storage, DLQ, X-Ray
- Data privacy: redacting PII in transit
- Data quality: required fields, schema validation, backfill

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo-code: Lambda processing Kinesis records
exports.handler = async (event) => {
  for (const rec of event.Records) {
    const payload = JSON.parse(Buffer.from(rec.kinesis.data, 'base64').toString('utf-8'));
    // validate
    if (!payload.deviceId || typeof payload.ts !== 'number' || typeof payload.metric !== 'number') {
      // send to DLQ
      continue;
    }
    // redact
    if (payload.email) payload.email = '[REDACTED]';
    if (payload.phone) payload.phone = '[REDACTED]';
    // dedupe check via DynamoDB (deviceId#ts)
    // write to S3 Parquet
  }
};
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test this end-to-end with LocalStack and simulate 2k events/min?
- What changes would you make to scale the deduplication and backfill strategy when ts is out of order?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to design robust, scalable ingestion with strong per-tenant data governance. Probes data quality enforcement, quarantine strategy, schema evolution, and backpressure handling under real-world load.

## Key Concepts

- Per-tenant data quality validation at ingestion
- Quarantine (bad records) with audit trails
- Schema evolution using Glue catalog and compatible formats
- Backpressure handling via DLQ and adaptive sampling
- Observability: per-tenant quality metrics and alerts

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudocode: per-tenant validation at ingress
function validateAndRoute(event, tenantConfig) {
  const validationResult = validateEvent(event, tenantConfig);

  if (validationResult.isValid) {
    writeToValidStream(event);
    updateMetrics(tenantConfig.tenantId, 'valid');
  } else {
    quarantineRecord(event, validationResult.errors, tenantConfig);
    updateMetrics(tenantConfig.tenantId, 'invalid');
  }
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical multi-tenant data isolation, deduping, and backfill in a beginner-friendly way.

## Key Concepts
- Multi-tenant isolation; partition keys; DynamoDB dedupe; Parquet on S3; DLQ; 3-day backfill; basic observability.

## Code Example
```javascript
// Example: Lambda handler snippet for JSON validation
const Ajv = require('ajv');
const ajv = new Ajv();
const schema = {/* minimal schema */};
exports.handler = async (e) => {
  const record = JSON.parse(Buffer.from(e.data, 'base64').toString());
  const valid = ajv.validate(schema, record);
  return { valid };
